    "lesson": {
      "title": "Survey size and uncertainty",
      "instruction": "Draw seeded repeated survey estimates and compare sample size with selection bias.",
      "explanation": "Independent draws with replacement from an effectively large population. Biased selection uses a stated response probability separate from population truth. Larger samples do not guarantee a closer individual estimate. No confidence intervals or finite-population correction."
